#
# Conformance case: profiles/probabilistic-dependency-joint
# AC (#506): marginals under a DECLARED dependency model (explicit joint), which
# must differ from the independence reading. Facts a and b are perfectly
# correlated: the joint table is { (a∧b): 0.5, (neither): 0.5 }. The rule
# both :- a, b gives P(both) = 0.5 under this joint — vs 0.5·0.5 = 0.25 if a and b
# were (wrongly) read as independent. This proves the declared joint is actually
# used. The model + joints + rule live in queries/both.logic.
#
# See README.md for the joint-outcome enumeration.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-dependency-joint/> .

ex:Condition a logic:Kind .
